"""Head vector-fit comparisons and runtime adapter status."""
import json
from research import OUT

def main():
    r=json.loads((OUT/'verification.json').read_text());renders=json.loads((OUT/'renders.json').read_text());views={}
    for row in renders['views']:views.setdefault(row['scope'],{}).setdefault(row['camera'],{})[row['stage']]=row['path']
    html='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><style>
body{font-family:var(--font-sans,system-ui);color:var(--foreground);line-height:1.45}p{margin:0 0 12px}.muted,small{color:var(--muted-foreground)}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:14px 0}select{font:inherit;color:var(--foreground);background:var(--background);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:7px;padding:8px;max-width:100%}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px}.caption{font-size:13px;margin-bottom:5px}.imagebox{aspect-ratio:1;background:#c3d2e0;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden}.imagebox img{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px;margin:14px 0}td,th{text-align:left;padding:8px 5px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.note{padding:16px;margin:14px 0;background:var(--secondary);border-radius:var(--radius,10px)}.note p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}small{font-size:12px}
</style></head><body>
<p><strong>Head vector fits: seven boxes and four convex hulls per Core.</strong> These replace five mesh owners while retaining their original part identities and transforms.</p>
<div class="controls"><select id="reference" aria-label="Reference"><option value="accepted">Accepted head collision</option><option value="visual">Approved visual appearance</option></select><select id="scope" aria-label="Scope"><option value="backing-strips">Four fitted backing strips</option><option value="rear-support">Seven-box rear support</option><option value="one-strip">One backing strip close-up</option><option value="head">Whole head</option></select><select id="camera" aria-label="Camera"><option value="back">Back</option><option value="front">Front</option><option value="left">Side</option></select></div>
<div class="pair"><div><p class="caption" id="beforeLabel"></p><div class="imagebox"><img id="before" alt="Accepted source geometry"></div></div><div><p class="caption">Primitive parameter preview</p><div class="imagebox"><img id="after" alt="Box and convex hull fits"></div></div></div>
<p class="muted" style="font-size:13px;margin-top:9px">Orange: selected source meshes. Blue: box shapes. Purple: convex hull shapes. Approved visuals remain byte-identical.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Per Core</th><th>Mesh triangles replaced</th><th>Primitive fit</th><th>Measured change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rear support</td><td>84</td><td>7 boxes</td><td>&lt;0.0001 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Four backing strips</td><td>577</td><td>4 convex hulls</td><td>0.81–1.61 mm</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><strong>1,322 additional mesh triangles move to vectors across both Cores.</strong> Each hull has 28–29 local vertices. Boxes are stored as half extents and a pose, with no triangle data required for the primitive.</p>
<div class="note"><p><strong>The fits are exported; runtime box/hull loading still needs enabling.</strong> The physics engine supports these native shapes, but the current field sidecar accepts cylinders only. The mixed review recipe uses a separate schema to keep that distinction explicit.</p><p>All 9,396 front-interface rays keep their first hit. All 96 rear-recess rays retain their depth within 0.001 mm. The existing 39 arm/base cylinders per Core stay exact.</p></div>
<p class="muted"><small>A bounded screen examined 65 head owners. Large single boxes/cylinders/hulls fill substantial slots or sockets; those meshes are retained. The four selected hulls close fine recesses or fastener gaps; their fit was checked using all vertices, centroids, edge midpoints and 50,000 area samples in each direction.</small></p>
<p class="muted"><small>Whole-field vector proposal: 444,187 retained mesh triangles + 78 cylinders + 14 boxes + 8 hulls. Diagnostic mesh alternative: 452,271 triangles. These alternatives are counted separately. The ordinary preview GLB still contains triangles; native parameters are in the mixed review recipe. No installation, commit, dynamic-contact or runtime-speed qualification.</small></p>
<script>const data=__DATA__,el=id=>document.getElementById(id);function show(){let s=el('scope').value,c=el('camera').value,r=el('reference').value,v=data[s][c];el('before').src=v[r];el('after').src=v.vectors;el('beforeLabel').textContent=el('reference').selectedOptions[0].textContent;}['reference','scope','camera'].forEach(id=>el(id).onchange=show);show();console.log('Head vectors: 7 boxes, 4 hulls per Core; 36 matched images');</script>
</body></html>'''
    (OUT/'gallery.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(views)))

if __name__=='__main__':main()
